1
00:00:00,535 --> 00:00:05,291
80 feet under a street in Manhattan
sits more gold than Fort Knox.

2
00:00:05,311 --> 00:00:09,571
Over 6,300 tons. Half a million bars.

3
00:00:09,591 --> 00:00:12,043
Worth over $800 billion.

4
00:00:12,063 --> 00:00:14,893
And almost none of it belongs to America.

5
00:00:14,913 --> 00:00:19,493
There's no front door. You walk in
through a 90-ton steel cylinder that

6
00:00:19,513 --> 00:00:21,052
turns to seal it shut.

7
00:00:21,072 --> 00:00:25,612
Inside are 122 locked
cages. One owner each.

8
00:00:25,632 --> 00:00:26,915
Mostly other countries.

9
00:00:26,935 --> 00:00:31,075
The workers who stack it wear magnesium
covers on their shoes, because one

10
00:00:31,095 --> 00:00:33,562
bar weighs 27 pounds.

11
00:00:33,582 --> 00:00:36,332
But here's the part nobody believes.

12
00:00:36,352 --> 00:00:40,136
When one country pays another
in gold, nothing gets shipped.

13
00:00:40,156 --> 00:00:44,476
A worker loads the bars onto a cart,
and wheels them to the cage next door.

14
00:00:44,496 --> 00:00:48,787
Billions change countries, and
the gold never leaves the room.

15
00:00:48,807 --> 00:00:53,067
The Fed charges no rent. And when a
country wants its gold back, it gets

16
00:00:53,087 --> 00:00:54,810
the exact same bars.

17
00:00:54,830 --> 00:00:57,540
So next time you walk down Liberty Street…

18
00:00:57,870 --> 00:00:58,950
look down.
